<title>HONG KONG: Korean French Bnk to set US$60 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Korean French Bnk to set US$60 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korean French Banking Corp has verbally mandated five banks to arrange a US$60 million floating rate certificate of deposit issue, bankers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said the facility has a final maturity of five years with a put and a call option in year three.</p>
<p>The issue will be priced at par to float at 50 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>The five mandated arrangers are Fuji International Finance, BFCE Singapore, KDB International Singapore, Bank Austria and Berliner Bank.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
